(619,1296,'A false belief regarding the self or persons or objects outside the self that persists despite the facts, and is not considered tenable by one&#39;s associates.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13292FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(620,1297,'A distinct and virulent form of DENGUE characterized by thrombocytopenia and hemoconcentration (grades I and II) and distinguished by a positive tourniquet test. When accompanied by circulatory failure and shock (grades III and IV), it is called dengue shock syndrome. (From Dorland, 28th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13287FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(621,1298,'A chronic endemic form of hypoplasia of the dental enamel caused by drinking water with a high fluorine content during the time of tooth formation, and characterized by defective calcification that gives a white chalky appearance to the enamel, which gradually undergoes brown discoloration. (Jablonski&#39;s Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p286)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13282FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(622,1299,'An autosomal dominant disorder of tooth development characterized by opalescent dentin resulting in discoloration of the teeth, ranging from dusky blue to brownish. The dentin is poorly formed with an abnormally low mineral content; the pulp canal is obliterated, but the enamel is normal. The teeth usually wear down rapidly, leaving short, brown stumps. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13277FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(623,1300,'A personality disorder characterized by a pervasive and excessive need to be taken care of that leads to submissive and clinging behavior and fears of separation, beginning by early adulthood and present in a variety of contexts. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13271FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(624,1301,'State in which an individual perceives or experiences a sensation of unreality concerning the self or the environment; it is seen in disorders such as schizophrenia, affection disorders, organic mental disorders, and personality disorders. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13269FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(625,1302,'An affective disorder manifested by either a dysphoric mood or loss of interest or pleasure in usual activities. The mood disturbance is prominent and relatively persistent.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13265FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(626,1305,'A situation in which the level of living of an individual, family, or group is below the standard of the community. It is often related to a specific income level.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13251FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(627,1306,'A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated. These behaviors include aggressive conduct that causes or threatens physical harm to other people or animals, nonagressive conduct that causes property loss or damage, deceitfulness or theft, and serious violations of rules. The onset is before age 18. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13250FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(628,1308,'A cognitive disorder marked by an impaired ability to comprehend or express language in its written or spoken form. This condition is caused by diseases which affect the language areas of the dominant hemisphere. Clinical features are used to classify the various subtypes of this condition. General categories include receptive, expressive, and mixed forms of aphasia.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13247FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(629,1309,'Diabetes mellitus characterized by insulin deficiency, sudden onset, severe hyperglycemia, rapid progression to ketoacidosis, and death unless treated with insulin. The disease may occur at any age, but is most common in childhood or adolescence.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13228FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(630,1310,'A heterogeneous group of disorders that share glucose intolerance in common.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13227FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(631,1311,'Protrusion of some part of the abdominal or retroperitoneal structures through the diaphragm into the thorax. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13193FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(632,1312,'Passage of excessively liquid or excessively frequent stools.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(633,1313,'Inability to urinate. The etiology of this disorder includes obstructive, neurogenic, pharmacologic, and psychogenic causes.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13181FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(634,1314,'A visual symptom in which a single object is perceived by the visual cortex as two objects rather than one. Disorders associated with this condition include REFRACTIVE ERRORS; STRABISMUS; OCULOMOTOR NERVE DISEASES; TROCHLEAR NERVE DISEASES; ABDUCENS NERVE DISEASES; and diseases of the BRAIN STEM and OCCIPITAL LOBE.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:53',NULL,NULL,'13149FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(635,1315,'A chronic form of cutaneous lupus erythematosus (LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS, CUTANEOUS) in which the skin lesions mimic those of the systemic form but in which systemic signs are rare. It is characterized by the presence of discoid skin plaques showing varying degrees of edema, erythema, scaliness, follicular plugging, and skin atrophy. Lesions are surrounded by an elevated erythematous border. The condition typically involves the face and scalp, but widespread dissemination may occur.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:46:54',NULL,NULL,'13144FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
