(1290,2730,'Disruption of structural continuity of the body as a result of the discharge of firearms.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5162FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1291,2731,'Lateral displacement of the great toe, producing deformity of the first metatarsophalangeal joint with callous, bursa, or bunion formation over the bony prominence.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5149FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1292,2732,'An extremely common benign tumor, occurring most commonly in infancy and childhood, made up of newly formed blood vessels, and resulting from malformation of angioblastic tissue of fetal life. It can occur anywhere in the body but is most frequently noticed in the skin and subcutaneous tissues. About 75% are present at birth, and about 60% occur in the head and neck area. The majority in infancy will regress spontaneously. Some hemangiomas grow rapidly during the early months of life and may be a source of some concern, although virtually all disappear by about 5 years of age. They do not metastasize and simple excision will often be curative. (Dorland, 27th ed; from Stedman, 25th ed; DeVita Jr et al., Cancer: Principles &amp;amp; Practice of Oncology, 3d ed, p1355)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5137FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1293,2733,'Bleeding into the joints. It may arise from trauma or spontaneously in patients with hemophilia.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5135FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1294,2734,'Frank bleeding in the gastrointestinal tract.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5132FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1295,2735,'Severe or complete loss of motor function on one side of the body. This condition is usually caused by BRAIN DISEASES that are localized to the cerebral hemisphere opposite to the side of weakness. Less frequently, BRAIN STEM lesions; cervical SPINAL CORD DISEASES; PERIPHERAL NERVOUS SYSTEM DISEASES; and other conditions may manifest as hemiplegia. The term hemiparesis (see PARESIS) refers to mild to moderate weakness involving one side of the body.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5125FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1296,2736,'A group of inherited disorders characterized by structural alterations within the hemoglobin molecule.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5114FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1297,2737,'A form of anemia in which the bone marrow fails to produce adequate numbers of peripheral blood elements.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5110FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1298,2740,'A self-limited hemorrhagic disorder of the first days of life, caused by a deficiency of the vitamin K-dependent blood coagulation factors II, VII, IX, and X. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5104FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1299,2741,'Severe inability of the liver to function normally, as evidenced by severe jaundice and abnormal levels of ammonia, bilirubin, alkaline phosphatase, glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase, lactic dehydrogenase, and reversal of the albumin/globulin ratio. (Blakiston&amp;amp;#39;s Gould Medical Dictionary, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5099FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1300,2742,'Protrusion of a loop or knuckle of an organ or tissue through an abnormal opening.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5079FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1301,2743,'Abnormal protrusion of the intestine through the abdominal muscles.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5077FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1302,2744,'A personality disorder characterized by overly reactive and intensely expressed or overly dramatic behavior, proneness to exaggeration, emotional excitability, and disturbances in interpersonal relationships.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:33',NULL,NULL,'5059FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1303,2745,'A malignant disease characterized by progressive enlargement of the lymph nodes, spleen, and general lymphoid tissue, and the presence of large, usually multinucleate, cells (REED-STERNBERG CELLS) of unknown origin.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'5058FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1304,2746,'A circumscribed collection of fluid, especially a collection of fluid in the tunica vaginalis of the testicle or along the spermatic cord. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'5047FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1305,2747,'A behavior disorder originating in childhood in which the essential features are signs of developmentally inappropriate inattention, impulsivity, and hyperactivity. Although most individuals have symptoms of both inattention and hyperactivity-impulsivity, one or the other pattern may be predominant. The disorder is more frequent in males than females. Onset is in childhood. Symptoms often attenuate during late adolescence although a minority experience the full complement of symptoms into mid-adulthood. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'5044FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1306,2749,'Disorders characterized by hypersomnolence during normal waking hours that may impair cognitive functioning. Subtypes include primary hypersomnia disorders (e.g., IDIOPATHIC HYPERSOMNOLENCE; NARCOLEPSY; and KLEINE-LEVIN SYNDROME) and secondary hypersomnia disorders where excessive somnolence can be attributed to a known cause (e.g., drug affect, MENTAL DISORDERS, and SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME). (From  J Neurol Sci 1998 Jan 8;153(2):192-202; Thorpy, Principles and Practice of Sleep Medicine, 2nd ed, p320)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'5014FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1307,2750,'Persistently high arterial blood pressure. Currently accepted threshold levels are 140 mm Hg systolic and 90 mm Hg diastolic pressure.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'5012FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1308,2751,'Hypertrophy or enlargement of the heart.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'5005FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1309,2752,'The condition that results from excessive loss of body water.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4978FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1310,2753,'Thrombocytopenia occurring in the absence of toxic exposure or a disease associated with decreased platelets. It is mediated by immune mechanisms, in most cases IgG autoantibodies which attach to platelets and subsequently undergo destruction by macrophages. The disease is seen in acute (affecting children) and chronic (adult) forms.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1311,2754,'Abortion in which not all the products of conception have been expelled.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4949FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1312,2755,'Failure of voluntary control of the anal sphincters, with involuntary passage of feces and flatus.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4948FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1313,2757,'Infections in birds and mammals produced by various species of Trichomonas.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4929FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1314,2758,'Inflammation of the uterine cervix.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'17322FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1315,2759,'Inflammation of the liver and liver disease involving degenerative or necrotic alterations of hepatocytes.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4889FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1316,2760,'Inflammation of the endometrium. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4887FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1317,2763,'Inflammation of the joint space(s).','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4881FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1318,2764,'Abnormal protrusion of the intestine into the inguinal canal.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4877FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1319,2768,'Dysfunction of one or more cranial nerves causally related to a traumatic injury. Penetrating and nonpenetrating CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; NECK INJURIES; and trauma to the facial region are conditions associated with cranial nerve injuries.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4873FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1320,2772,'This concept includes injury of liver or gallbladder','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'17101FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1321,2779,'Bleeding into a cerebral hemisphere of the brain, including lobar, subcortical white matter, and basal ganglia hemorrhages. Commonly associated conditions include HYPERTENSION; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOSCLEROSIS; INTRACRANIAL ANEURYSM; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOVENOUS MALFORMATIONS; CEREBRAL AMYLOID ANGIOPATHY; and CEREBRAL INFARCTION.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4828FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1322,2781,'Uterine bleeding, usually irregular or acyclic, between periods.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:34',NULL,NULL,'4805FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1323,2784,'Injuries to tissues caused by contact with heat, steam, chemicals (BURNS, CHEMICAL), electricity (BURNS, ELECTRIC), or the like.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4775FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1324,2785,'Symmetrical osteitis of the four limbs, chiefly localized to the phalanges and the terminal epiphyses of the long bones of the forearm and leg, sometimes extending to the proximal ends of the limbs and the flat bones, and accompanied by dorsal kyphosis and joint involvement. It is often secondary to chronic conditions of the lungs and heart. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4757FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1325,2786,'Calculi occurring in the kidney. Calculi too large to pass spontaneously range in size from 1 cm to the staghorn stones that occupy the renal pelvis and calyces.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4753FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1326,2787,'Abnormally increased convexity in the curvature of the thoracic spine as viewed from the side. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4743FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1327,2788,'Disturbances in sexual desire and the psychophysiologic changes that characterize the sexual response cycle and cause marked distress and interpersonal difficulty. (APA, DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4737FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1328,2789,'Increase in the mass of bone per unit volume.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4730FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1329,2794,'A syndrome characterized by persistent or recurrent fatigue, diffuse musculoskeletal pain, sleep disturbances, and subjective cognitive impairment of 6 months duration or longer. Symptoms are not caused by ongoing exertion; are not relieved by rest; and result in a substantial reduction of previous levels of occupational, educational, social, or personal activities. Minor alterations of immune, neuroendocrine, and autonomic function may be associated with this syndrome. There is also considerable overlap between this condition and FIBROMYALGIA. (From Semin Neurol 1998;18(2):237-42; Ann Intern Med 1994 Dec 15;121(12): 953-9)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4710FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1330,2795,'A chronic, atrophic skin disease characterized by white, angular, flat, well-defined, indurated papules with an erythematous halo and follicular, black, keratotic plugs. It is the most common cause of kraurosis vulvae in females and balanitis xerotica obliterans in males. It is called also white spot disease and Csillag&#39;s disease. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4702FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1331,2797,'Fibrous, bony, cartilaginous and osteocartilaginous fragments in a synovial joint. Major causes are osteochondritis dissecans, synovial chondromatosis, osteophytes, fractured articular surfaces and damaged menisci.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4682FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1332,2798,'The anterior concavity in the curvature of the lumbar and cervical spine as viewed from the side. The term usually refers to abnormally increased curvature (hollow back, saddle back, swayback). It does not include lordosis as normal mating posture in certain animals ( = POSTURE + SEX BEHAVIOR, ANIMAL).','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4681FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1333,2800,'Leukemia associated with hyperplasia and overactivity of the lymphoid tissue. There are increased numbers of circulating malignant lymphocytes and lymphoblasts. (Dorland, 28th ed, p919)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4660FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1334,2802,'A protozoan disease caused by four species of the genus PLASMODIUM (P. falciparum (MALARIA, FALCIPARUM), P. vivax (MALARIA, VIVAX), P. ovale, and P. malariae) and transmitted by the bite of an infected female mosquito of the genus Anopheles. Malaria is endemic in parts of Asia, Africa, Central and South America, Oceania, and certain Caribbean islands. It is characterized by extreme exhaustion associated with paroxysms of high fever, sweating, shaking chills, and anemia.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4638FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1335,2804,'A malignant neoplasm derived from cells that are capable of forming melanin, which may occur in the skin of any part of the body, in the eye, or, rarely, in the mucous membranes of the genitalia, anus, oral cavity, or other sites. It occurs mostly in adults and may originate de novo or from a pigmented nevus or malignant lentigo. Melanomas frequently metastasize widely, and the regional lymph nodes, liver, lungs, and brain are likely to be involved. The incidence of malignant skin melanomas is rising rapidly in all parts of the world. (Stedman, 25th ed; from Rook et al., Textbook of Dermatology, 4th ed, p2445)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4605FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1336,2805,'A primary or metastatic malignant neoplasm involving the uterine corpus.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4602FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1337,2806,'Tumors or cancer of the endocrine glands in general or unspecified.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4600FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1338,2807,'Tumors or cancer of the pancreas.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4581FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1339,2808,'Tumors or cancer of the STOMACH.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4576FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1340,2810,'Cancer of the gums.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4561FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1341,2811,'Tumors or cancer of the LIP.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4558FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1342,2812,'Tumors or cancer of the SALIVARY GLANDS.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4551FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1343,2813,'Cancer or tumors of the bladder.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4532FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1344,2814,'Such malposition and contact of the maxillary and mandibular teeth as to interfere with the highest efficiency during the excursive movements of the jaw that are essential for mastication. (Jablonski, Illustrated Dictionary of Dentistry, 1982)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:35',NULL,NULL,'4528FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1345,2817,'A highly contagious infectious disease caused by MORBILLIVIRUS, common among children but also seen in the nonimmune of any age, in which the virus enters the respiratory tract via droplet nuclei and multiplies in the epithelial cells, spreading throughout the reticuloendothelial system. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4517FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1346,2819,'Syndrome caused by sucking of thick meconium into the lungs, usually by term or post-term infants (often small for gestational age) either in utero or with first breath. The resultant small airway obstruction may produce respiratory distress, tachypnea, cyanosis, pneumothorax, and/or pneumomediastinum.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4514FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1347,2823,'Disturbances in registering an impression, in the retention of an acquired impression, or in the recall of an impression. Memory impairments are associated with DEMENTIA; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; ENCEPHALITIS; ALCOHOLISM (see also ALCOHOL AMNESTIC DISORDER); SCHIZOPHRENIA; and other conditions.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4504FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1348,2827,'Subnormal intellectual functioning which originates during the developmental period. This has multiple potential etiologies, including genetic defects and perinatal insults. Intelligence quotient (IQ) scores are commonly used to determine whether an individual is mentally retarded. IQ scores between 70 and 79 are in the borderline mentally retarded range. Scores below 67 are in the retarded range. (Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p28)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4487FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1349,2828,'Generic term for diseases caused by an abnormal metabolic process. It can be congenital due to inherited enzyme abnormality (METABOLISM, INBORN ERRORS) or acquired due to disease of an endocrine organ or failure of a metabolically important organ such as the liver. (Stedman, 26th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1350,2831,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4467FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1351,2832,'Abnormal protrusion of one or both of the leaflets of the mitral valve into the left atrium during systole. This may be accompanied by mitral regurgitation, systolic murmur, nonejection click, or cardiac arrhythmia.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4448FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1352,2836,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4445FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1353,2839,'Fractures in which the break in bone is not accompanied by an external wound.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4385FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1354,2843,'Form of leukemia characterized by an uncontrolled proliferation of the myeloid lineage and their precursors in the bone marrow and other sites.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1355,2845,'Gross necrosis of the myocardium, as a result of interruption of the blood supply to the area. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4326FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1356,2847,'Inflammation of the muscular walls of the heart. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4324FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1357,2848,'A major deviation from normal patterns of behavior.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4312FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1358,2849,'A condition characterized by recurrent episodes of daytime somnolence and lapses in consciousness (microsomnias) that may be associated with automatic behaviors and AMNESIA. CATAPLEXY; SLEEP PARALYSIS, and hypnagogic HALLUCINATIONS frequently accompany narcolepsy. The pathophysiology of this disorder includes sleep-onset rapid eye movement (REM) sleep, which normally follows stage III or IV sleep. (From Neurology 1998 Feb;50(2 Suppl 1):S2-S7)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4310FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1359,2850,'Focal accumulations of edema fluid in the nasal mucosa accompanied by hyperplasia of the associated submucosal connective tissue. Polyps may be neoplasms, foci of inflammation, degenerative lesions, or malformations.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:36',NULL,NULL,'4306FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1360,2852,'A transient unconjugated hyperbilirubinemia that occurs between the second and fifth days of life because the hepatic enzyme GLUCURONOSYLTRANSFERASE required for BILIRUBIN detoxification is inadquedate.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4296FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1361,2856,'Neoplasms of the intracranial components of the central nervous system, including the cerebral hemispheres, basal ganglia, hypothalamus, thalamus, brain stem, and cerebellum. Brain neoplasms are subdivided into primary (originating from brain tissue) and secondary (i.e., metastatic) forms. Primary neoplasms are subdivided into benign and malignant forms. In general, brain tumors may also be classified by age of onset, histologic type, or presenting location in the brain.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4292FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1362,2858,'Clinical association of heavy proteinuria, hypoalbuminemia, and generalized edema.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4268FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1363,2862,'A general term indicating inflammation of a peripheral or cranial nerve. Clinical manifestation may include PAIN; PARESTHESIAS; PARESIS; or HYPESTHESIA.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4259FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1364,2863,'Diseases of the peripheral nerves external to the brain and spinal cord, which includes diseases of the nerve roots, ganglia, plexi, autonomic nerves, sensory nerves, and motor nerves.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4246FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1365,2865,'Failure or imperfection of vision at night or in dim light, with good vision only on bright days. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4240FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1366,2866,'Involuntary discharge of urine after the age at which urinary control should have been achieved; often used alone with specific reference to involuntary discharge of urine occurring during sleep at night (bed-wetting; nocturnal enuresis). (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4239FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1367,2867,'Patient or client refusal of or resistance to medical, psychological, or psychiatric treatment. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4221FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1368,2873,'An enlarged thyroid gland containing circumscribed nodules within its substance. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4208FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1369,2874,'Hemorrhage into the peritoneal cavity.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4207FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1370,2875,'Union of the fragments of a fractured bone in a faulty or abnormal position. If two bones parallel to one another unite by osseous tissue, the result is a crossunion. (From Manual of Orthopaedic Terminology, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4206FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1371,2876,'A fracture in which union fails to occur, the ends of the bone becoming rounded and eburnated, and a false joint occurs. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4205FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1372,2880,'Involuntary movements of the eye that are divided into two types, jerk and pendular. Jerk nystagmus has a slow phase in one direction followed by a corrective fast phase in the opposite direction, and is usually caused by central or peripheral vestibular dysfunction. Pendular nystagmus features oscillations that are of equal velocity in both directions and this condition is often associated with visual loss early in life. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p272)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4196FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1373,2881,'Increase in body weight beyond skeletal and physical standards as the result of an excessive accumulation of fat in the body. More than two times the ideal weight is considered OBESITY, MORBID.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4194FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1374,2882,'Abnormally infrequent menstruation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:37',NULL,NULL,'4172FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1375,2888,'Fractures of the femur.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4165FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1376,2891,'diarrheal illness, usually due to infection','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'151FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1377,2895,'Pathologic process consisting of a partial or complete disruption of the layers of a surgical wound.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4093FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1378,2896,'Disorders related or resulting from abuse or mis-use of opioids.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4090FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1379,2898,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1380,2899,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4077FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1381,2900,'A progressive, degenerative joint disease, the most common form of arthritis, especially in older persons. The disease is thought to result not from the aging process but from biochemical changes and biomechanical stresses affecting articular cartilage. In the foreign literature it is often called osteoarthrosis deformans.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4067FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1382,2908,'A genus of parasitic nematodes whose organisms are distributed in Central and South America. Characteristics include a smooth cuticle and an enlarged anterior end.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4027FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1383,2910,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'4020FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1384,2912,'Movements or behaviors associated with sleep, sleep stages, or partial arousals from sleep that may impair sleep maintenance. Parasomnias are generally divided into four groups: arousal disorders, sleep-wake transition disorders, parasomnias of REM sleep, and nonspecific parasomnias. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p191)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'3998FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1385,2913,'Clinical or subclinical disturbances of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, excessive, and disorganized discharge of brain cells. Clinical manifestations include abnormal motor, sensory and psychic phenomena. Recurrent seizures are usually referred to as EPILEPSY or \"seizure disorder.\"','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'3987FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1386,2914,'Fractures occurring as a result of disease of a bone or from some undiscoverable cause, and not due to trauma. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'3985FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1387,2918,'Abnormal enlargement or overgrowth of the gingivae brought about by enlargement of existing cells.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'3968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1388,2921,'Conditions in which increased pressure within a limited space compromises the circulation and function of tissue within that space. Compartmentation involves mainly the leg but also involved are the forearm, arm, thigh, shoulder, and buttock. Some of the causes of increased pressure are trauma, tight dressings, hemorrhage, and exercise. Sequelae include nerve compression, paralysis, and contracture.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'3959FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1389,2922,'General or unspecified diseases of the blood vessels outside the heart. It is for diseases of the peripheral as opposed to the cardiac circulation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:38',NULL,NULL,'3957FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1390,2923,'Inflammation of the lining of the abdomen and pelvis.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3953FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1391,2924,'A major deviation from normal patterns of behavior.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3950FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1392,2928,'Inflammation of a vein associated with thrombus formation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3941FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1393,2929,'Psychiatric illness or diseases manifested by breakdowns in the adaptational process expressed primarily as abnormalities of thought, feeling, and behavior producing either distress or impairment of function.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'15797FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1394,2930,'Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3937FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1395,2938,'A placenta which develops in the lower uterine segment, in the zone of dilatation, so that it covers or adjoins the internal os. Painless hemorrhage in the last trimester, particularly during the eighth month, is the most common symptom. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3920FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1396,2939,'A condition or physical state produced by the ingestion, injection or inhalation of, or exposure to a deleterious agent.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3907FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1397,2941,'A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated. These behaviors include aggressive conduct that causes or threatens physical harm to other people or animals, nonagressive conduct that causes property loss or damage, deceitfulness or theft, and serious violations of rules. The onset is before age 18. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'15717FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1398,2942,'Infection occurring at the site of a surgical incision.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3865FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1399,2945,'Anxiety disorders manifested by the development of characteristic symptoms following a psychologically traumatic event that is outside the normal range of usual human experience. Symptoms include re-experiencing the traumatic event and numbing of responsiveness to or reduced involvement with the external world.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3854FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1400,2949,'Onset of labor before term but after the fetus has become viable, usually sometime during the 29th through 38th week of gestation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3846FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1401,2950,'Disturbances in sexual desire and the psychophysiologic changes that characterize the sexual response cycle and cause marked distress and interpersonal difficulty. (APA, DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'15704FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1402,2952,'Hereditary metabolic disorder characterized by recurrent acute arthritis, hyperuricemia and deposition of sodium urate in and around the joints, sometimes with formation of uric acid calculi.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:39',NULL,NULL,'3823FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1403,2955,'Tumors or cancer of the biliary tract.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3818FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1404,2956,'Neoplasms of the intracranial components of the central nervous system, including the cerebral hemispheres, basal ganglia, hypothalamus, thalamus, brain stem, and cerebellum. Brain neoplasms are subdivided into primary (originating from brain tissue) and secondary (i.e., metastatic) forms. Primary neoplasms are subdivided into benign and malignant forms. In general, brain tumors may also be classified by age of onset, histologic type, or presenting location in the brain.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3816FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1405,2958,'Tumors or cancer of the EYE.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3813FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1406,2959,'Tumors or cancer of the breast.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3811FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1407,2960,'Tumors or cancers of the KIDNEY.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3802FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1408,2962,'Tumors or cancer of the INTESTINES.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3779FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1409,2963,'Tumors or cancer of the TONGUE.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3775FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1410,2965,'The primary sore of syphilis, a painless indurated, eroded papule, occurring at the site of entry of the infection.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3761FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1411,2966,'Subnormal intellectual functioning which originates during the developmental period. This has multiple potential etiologies, including genetic defects and perinatal insults. Intelligence quotient (IQ) scores are commonly used to determine whether an individual is mentally retarded. IQ scores between 70 and 79 are in the borderline mentally retarded range. Scores below 67 are in the retarded range. (Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p28)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3740FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1412,2972,'Embolism in the pulmonary artery or one of its branches.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3688FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1413,2973,'Tuberculosis of the lungs.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3678FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1414,2974,'Tuberculosis of the lungs.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1415,2975,'Purplish or brownish red discoloration, easily visible through the epidermis, caused by hemorrhage into the tissues.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3669FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1416,2977,'A cutaneous inflammatory reaction occurring as a result of exposure to ionizing radiation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3661FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1417,2979,'Condition characterized by splenomegaly, some reduction in the number of circulating blood cells in the presence of a normal or hyperactive bone marrow, and the potential for reversal by splenectomy.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3652FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1418,2983,'The inability of a kidney to excrete metabolites at normal plasma levels under conditions of normal loading, or the inability to retain electrolytes under conditions of normal intake. In the acute form (KIDNEY FAILURE, ACUTE), it is marked by uremia and usually by oliguria or anuria, with hyperkalemia and pulmonary edema. The chronic form (KIDNEY FAILURE, CHRONIC) is irreversible and requires hemodialysis.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1419,2984,'A childhood seizure disorder characterized by rhythmic electrical brain discharges of geneneralized onset. Clinical features include a sudden cessation of ongoing activity usually without loss of postural tone. Rhythmic blinking of the eyelids or lip smacking frequently accompanies the seizure. The usual duration is 5-10 seconds, and multiple episodes may occur daily. Juvenile absence epilepsy is characterized by the juvenile onset of absence seizures and an increased incidence of myoclonus and tonic-clonic seizures. (Menkes, Textbook of Child Neurology, 5th ed, p736)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'15623FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1420,2985,'Infection of the nose, sinuses, trachea (windpipe), bronchi, bronchioles or lungs.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:40',NULL,NULL,'3628FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1421,2991,'An acute, usually benign, infectious disease caused by the RUBELLA VIRUS and most often affecting children and nonimmune young adults, in which the virus enters the respiratory tract via droplet nuclei and spreads to the lymphatic system. (From Dorland, 27th edition)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1422,2992,'Sudden calamitous events producing great material damage, loss, and distress. They are the result of natural phenomena such as earthquakes, floods, etc.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'15611FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1423,2996,'Disorders in which there is a loss of ego boundaries or a gross impairment in reality testing with delusions or prominent hallucinations. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3566FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1424,2997,'A personality disorder in which there are oddities of thought (magical thinking, paranoid ideation, suspiciousness), perception (illusions, depersonalization), speech (digressive, vague, overelaborate), and behavior (inappropriate affect in social interactions, frequently social isolation) that are not severe enough to characterize schizophrenia.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3564FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1425,2998,'A chronic, progressive dermatosis characterized by boardlike hardening and immobility of the affected skin, with visceral involvement, especially of lungs, esophagus, kidneys and heart. It may be accompanied by calcinosis, Raynaud&#39;s phenomenon, and telangiectasis (CREST syndrome). It includes acrosclerosis and sclerodactyly.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3557FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1426,2999,'Inflammation of the mucous membrane of the nose similar to that found in hay fever except that symptoms persist throughout the year. The causes are usually air-borne allergens, particularly dusts, feathers, molds, animal fur, etc.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3552FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1427,3000,'A chronic inflammatory disease of the skin of unknown etiology. It is characterized by moderate erythema, dry, moist, or greasy scaling, and yellow crusted patches on various areas, especially the scalp. On the scalp, it generally appears first as small patches of scales, progressing to involve the entire scalp with exfoliation of excessive amounts of dry scales (dandruff).','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3550FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1428,3002,'A general term referring to sudden and often violent motor activity of cerebral or brainstem origin. Convulsions may also occur in the absence of an electrical cerebral discharge (e.g., in response to hypotension).','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3527FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1429,3003,'Systemic disease associated with the presence and persistence of pathogenic microorganisms or their toxins in the blood. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3517FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1430,3005,'Infection of the nose, sinuses, trachea (windpipe), bronchi, bronchioles or lungs.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3513FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1431,3006,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3509FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1432,3007,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3507FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1433,3009,'A skin condition characterized by the development of recurring boils.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'112FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1434,3010,'A pathological condition that can suddenly affect the hemodynamic equilibrium, usually manifested by failure to perfuse or oxygenate vital organs.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3499FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1435,3011,'Difficult childbirth or labor.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3497FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1436,3012,'A transient loss of consciousness and postural tone caused by diminished blood flow to the brain (i.e., BRAIN ISCHEMIA). Presyncope refers to the sensation of lightheadedness and loss of strength that precedes a syncopal event or accompanies an incomplete syncope. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp367-9)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1437,3013,'Conditions characterized by disturbances of usual sleep patterns or behaviors. Sleep disorders may be divided into three major categories: DYSSOMNIAS (i.e. disorders characterized by insomnia or hypersomnia), PARASOMNIAS (abnormal sleep behaviors), and sleep disorders secondary to medical or psychiatric disorders. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p187)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3474FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1438,3015,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'15592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1439,3019,'A cognitive disorder characterized by an impaired ability to comprehend written and printed words or phrases despite intact vision. This condition may be developmental or acquired. Developmental dyslexia is marked by reading achievement that falls substantially below that expected given the individual&#39;s chronological age, measured intelligence, and age-appropriate education. The disturbance in reading significantly interferes with academic achievement or with activities of daily living that require reading skills. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'3450FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1440,3022,'A type of acneiform disorder in which secondary pyogenic infection in and around pilosebaceous structures ends in keloidal scarring. It manifests as persistent folliculitis of the back of the neck associated with occlusion of the follicular orifices. It is most often encountered in black or Asian men.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'15583FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1441,3023,'A chronic disorder of the pilosebaceous apparatus associated with an increase in sebum secretion. It is characterized by open comedones (blackheads), closed comedones (whiteheads), and pustular nodules. The cause is unknown, but heredity and age are predisposing factors.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:41',NULL,NULL,'15578FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1442,3025,'Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3430FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1443,3028,'A collective term for muscle and ligament injuries without dislocation or fracture. A sprain is a joint injury in which some of the fibers of a supporting ligament are ruptured but the continuity of the ligament remains intact. A strain is an overstretching or overexertion of some part of the musculature.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3426FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1444,3030,'A disease of infants due to group 2 phage type 17 staphylococci that produce an epidermolytic exotoxin. Superficial fine vesicles and bullae form and rupture easily, resulting in loss of large sheets of epidermis.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3417FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1445,3032,'Skin diseases characterized by local or general distributions of blisters. They are classified according to the site and mode of blister formation. Lesions can appear spontaneously or be precipitated by infection, trauma, or sunlight. Etiologies include immunologic and genetic factors. (From Scientific American Medicine, 1990)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3378FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1446,3034,'Disorders related to substance abuse, the side effects of a medication, toxin exposure, and alcohol related disorders','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3374FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1447,3036,'General or unspecified injuries involving the fingers.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'15538FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1448,3039,'Clinical syndrome characterized by abdominal pain of great severity associated with other symptoms and signs, usually those of acute peritonitis, which might well be the result of a ruptured abdominal viscus or a similar abdominal catastrophe requiring urgent surgical operation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'15521FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1449,3042,'A chronic, relapsing, inflammatory, and often febrile multisystemic disorder of connective tissue, characterized principally by involvement of the skin, joints, kidneys, and serosal membranes. It is of unknown etiology, but is thought to represent a failure of the regulatory mechanisms of the autoimmune system. The disease is marked by a wide range of system dysfunctions, an elevated erythrocyte sedimentation rate, and the formation of LE cells in the blood or bone marrow.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3347FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1450,3046,'Acute inflammation of the vermiform appendix.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'15511FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1451,3047,'A variety of conditions affecting the anatomic and functional characteristics of the temporomandibular joint. Factors contributing to the complexity of temporomandibular diseases are its relation to dentition and mastication and the symptomatic effects in other areas which account for referred pain to the joint and the difficulties in applying traditional diagnostic procedures to temporomandibular joint pathology where tissue is rarely obtained and x-rays are often inadequate or nonspecific. Common diseases are developmental abnormalities, trauma, subluxation, luxation, arthritis, and neoplasia. (From Thoma&#39;s Oral Pathology, 6th ed, pp577-600)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3339FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1452,3048,'Inflammation of the bronchioles. Including acute bronchiolitis due to respiratory syncitial virus, human metapneumovirus, other specified organisms or unspecified.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'15502FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1453,3049,'Downward displacement of the uterus. It is classified in various degrees: in the first degree the cervix is within the vaginal orifice; in the second degree the cervix is outside the orifice; in the third degree the entire uterus is outside the orifice.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3331FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1454,3050,'The presence of abnormal uterine bleeding immediately after labor or childbirth.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3330FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1455,3051,'Condition of vaginal bleeding with or without pain in early pregnancy which may presage an abortion.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1456,3052,'Disorders in which the symptoms are distressing to the individual and recognized by him or her as being unacceptable. Social relationships may be greatly affected but usually remain within acceptable limits. The disturbance is relatively enduring or recurrent without treatment.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3328FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1457,3053,'A decrease in the number of blood platelets.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3326FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1458,3054,'Inflammation of the thyroid gland.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3317FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1459,3055,'DEF: Frequent and loose bowel movements of acute onset (&amp;lt; 24 hours).  DESC: Commonly associated with abdominal pain. May be associated with blood or mucus in the stool. REF: http://www.healthatoz.com/healthatoz/Atoz/common/standard/transform.jsp?requestURI=/healthatoz/Atoz/ency/diarrhea.jsp','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'15491FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1460,3056,'Clinical or subclinical disturbances of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, excessive, and disorganized discharge of brain cells. Clinical manifestations include abnormal motor, sensory and psychic phenomena. Recurrent seizures are usually referred to as EPILEPSY or seizure disorder','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3302FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1461,3057,'A focal dystonia characterized by a sustained spasmodic contraction of neck muscles. The trapezius and sternocleidomastoid muscles are primarily involved, resulting in twisting of the neck and an unnatural position of the head. Torticollis may occur as a primary disease process or in association with another condition (e.g., NECK INJURIES, the use of ANTIPSYCHOTIC AGENTS, etc.). (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p107)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3297FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1462,3058,'ToxÃ©mie GravÃ©dique','fr',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3295FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1463,3058,'Pregnancy-induced hypertensive states, including EPH gestosis when edema and proteinuria accompany hypertension. Other hypertensive disorders that develop during pregnancy or the puerperium are pre-eclampsia and eclampsia, either of which may be superimposed upon chronic hypertensive vascular or renal disease.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:42',NULL,NULL,'3294FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1465,3060,'Inflammation of the lining of the stomach and intestines, often accompanied by diarrhea.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'15476FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1467,3063,'A microscopically inflammatory, usually reversible, patchy hair loss occurring in sharply defined areas and usually involving the beard or scalp. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'3271FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1469,3066,'General or unspecified injuries involving the foot.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'3268FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1470,3067,'Compulsion to pull out one&amp;#39;s hair.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'3261FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1471,3069,'A subgroup of PARAPSORIASIS itself divided into acute and chronic forms. The acute form is characterized by the abrupt onset of a generalized, reddish-brown, maculopapular eruption. Lesions may be vesicular, hemorrhagic, crusted, or necrotic. Histologically the disease is characterized by epidermal necrolysis. The chronic form shows milder skin changes with necrosis. An important variant of the chronic form is LYMPHOMATOID PAPULOSIS.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'15451FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1472,3070,'Mycobacterial infection of the bone','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'16793FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1473,3071,'Inflammation of the tonsils of varying degrees of severity and involving simple inflammation.  Associated with acute pharyngitis, streptococcus infection, or formation of an abscess (as quinsy).','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'111FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1474,3073,'Infection of the lymph nodes by tuberculosis. Tuberculous infection of the cervical lymph nodes is scrofula.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'3100FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1475,3077,'Inflammation of the middle ear.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'15396FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1476,3078,'Ulceration of the skin and underlying structures of the lower extremity. About 90% of the cases are due to venous insufficiency (VARICOSE ULCER), 5% to arterial disease, and the remaining 5% to other causes.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'3016FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1477,3079,'A loss of mucous substance of the mouth showing local excavation of the surface, resulting from the sloughing of inflammatory necrotic tissue. It is the result of a variety of causes, e.g., denture irritation, aphthous stomatitis (STOMATITIS, APHTHOUS), NOMA, necrotizing gingivitis (GINGIVITIS, NECROTIZING, ULCERATIVE), TOOTHBRUSHING, and various irritants. (From Jablonski, Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p842)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'3012FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1478,3081,'The protrusion of part of the intestine at the umbilicus (Dorland, 27th ed).','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'3008FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1479,3084,'Inflammation of the prostate. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'15383FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1480,3086,'Infections affecting those structures of the body which participate in the secretion and elimination of urine, i.e., the kidney, the ureters, the urinary bladder, and the urethra.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'2993FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1481,3087,'Inflammation or infection of the kidney.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:43',NULL,NULL,'15379FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1482,3090,'Failure to adequately provide oxygen to cells of the body and to remove excess carbon dioxide from them. (Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15374FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1483,3091,'An illusion of movement, either of the external world revolving around the individual or of the individual revolving in space. Vertigo may be associated with disorders of the inner ear, vestibular nerve, brainstem, and cerebral cortex. Lesions in the temporal and parietal lobes may be associated with FOCAL SEIZURES that may feature vertigo as an ictal manifestation. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp300-1)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'2957FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1485,3097,'DEF: An acute infectious disease of the liver caused by the hepatitis A virus. DESC: Most commonly transmitted by the faecal-oral route, such as contaminated food. Incubation period 4-6 weeks. REF: {http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hepatitis_A }','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15358FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1486,3098,'An acute or chronic gingival infection characterized by redness and swelling, necrosis extending from the interdental papillae along the gingival margins, pain, hemorrhage, necrotic odor, and often a pseudomembrane. The condition may extend to the oral mucosa, tongue, palate, or pharynx.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15356FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1487,3099,'A catarrhal disorder of the upper respiratory tract, which may be viral, a mixed infection, or an allergic reaction. It is marked by acute coryza, slight rise in temperature, chilly sensations, and general indisposition. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15354FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1488,3102,'Inflammation of a bursa, occasionally accompanied by a calcific deposit in the underlying supraspinatus tendon. The most common site is the subdeltoid bursa. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15342FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1490,3106,'Obsessive, persistent, intense fear of open places.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15295FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1491,3108,'Spontaneous autoamputation of the fourth or fifth toe.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15289FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1492,3109,'Inflammation of the stomach lining','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'16751FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1494,3115,'A microscopically inflammatory, usually reversible, patchy hair loss occurring in sharply defined areas and usually involving the beard or scalp. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15241FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1495,3118,'A degenerative disease of the brain characterized by the insidious onset of dementia. Impairment of memory, judgement, attention span, and problem solving skills are followed by severe APRAXIA and a global loss of cognitive abilities. The condition primarily occurs after age 60, and is marked pathologically by severe cortical atrophy and the triad of SENILE PLAQUES; NEUROFIBRILLARY TANGLES; and NEUROPIL THREADS. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp1049-57)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15225FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1496,3121,'An autosomal dominant or X-linked disorder in which there is faulty development of the dental enamel owing to agenesis, hypoplasia, or hypocalcification of the enamel. It is marked by enamel that is very thin and friable and frequently stained in various shades of brown. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15208FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1497,3122,'Absence of menstruation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15207FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1498,3124,'Disorders characterized by multiple cessations of respirations during sleep that induce partial arousals and interfere with the maintenance of sleep. Sleep apnea syndromes are divided into central (see SLEEP APENA, CENTRAL), obstructive (see SLEEP APNEA, OBSTRUCTIVE), and mixed central-obstructive types.','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'2800FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1499,3125,'A painful linear ulcer at the margin of the anus. It appears as a crack or slit in the mucous membrane of the anus and is very painful and difficult to heal. (Dorland, 27th ed &amp; Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 10:47:44',NULL,NULL,'15175FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
